viewer panel (the deterministic floor itself shipped in #140's floor slice). The one case that still degrades to the built-in single `code-quality` reviewer + a `[Friction]` is an **explicit** selection that resolves to **no known reviewers** (a name matching neither the pool nor a canonical persona) — a typo must not silently escalate to the profile panel. An explicit selection that *does* resolve wins outright.
